{"name":"Reptile Revenge","hex":"#5e582b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"reptile","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A (typically scaly and egg-laying) cold-blooded vertebrate tetrapod animal, of the class Reptilia (excluding birds), such as a lizard, turtle, snake, crocodile, alligator, etc. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Any member of the class Reptilia, including birds."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Creeping; moving on the belly, or by means of small and short legs.","Grovelling; low; vulgar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reptile"},{"term":"revenge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any form of personal, retaliatory action against an individual, institution, or group for some alleged or perceived harm or injustice.","A win by a previous loser."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take revenge for (a particular harmful action) or on behalf of (its victim); to avenge.","To take one's revenge (on or upon someone)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revenge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Reptile","blocks":[{"text":"Reptiles, as commonly defined, are tetrapod vertebrate animals with an ectothermic metabolism and amniotic development. Reptiles traditionally comprise four orders: Testudines (turtles), Crocodilia, Squamata and Rhynchocephalia (tuatara), with about 12,000 extant species listed in the Reptile Database. The study of the traditional reptile orders, customarily in combination with the study of modern amphibians, is called herpetology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/TWC_Wildlife_Centre%E2%80%A2_Stewart_Nimmo_%E2%80%A2_MRD_8910.jpg/330px-TWC_Wildlife_Centre%E2%80%A2_Stewart_Nimmo_%E2%80%A2_MRD_8910.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reptile","wikidata":"Q10811"},{"title":"Revenge","blocks":[{"text":"Revenge is an act against a person or group in response to a grievance, be it real or perceived. Vengeful forms of justice, such as primitive justice or retributive justice, are often differentiated from more formal and refined forms of justice such as distributive justice or restorative justice."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Peinture_Palais_de_Justice_de_Toulouse.jpg/330px-Peinture_Palais_de_Justice_de_Toulouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Revenge","wikidata":"Q1712140"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/SaltwaterCrocodile%28%27Maximo%27%29.jpg/500px-SaltwaterCrocodile%28%27Maximo%27%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/SaltwaterCrocodile%28%27Maximo%27%29.jpg/500px-SaltwaterCrocodile%28%27Maximo%27%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaltwaterCrocodile('Maximo').jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Florida_Box_Turtle_Digon3.jpg/500px-Florida_Box_Turtle_Digon3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Florida_Box_Turtle_Digon3.jpg/1280px-Florida_Box_Turtle_Digon3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Florida_Box_Turtle_Digon3.jpg/500px-Florida_Box_Turtle_Digon3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlorida_Box_Turtle_Digon3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Rhinechis_scalaris_cropped.jpg/500px-Rhinechis_scalaris_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail